level PAT (the standalone holding entity) grew strongly: LKR 1.36bn for Q2 2026 vs LKR 882m in Q2 2025 (+54% YoY) and vs a derived LKR 540m in Q1 2026 (+152% QoQ), driven by a 32% jump in Revenue and a 45% jump in Operating Profit, plus a large exchange gain (LKR 164m vs LKR 25m a year earlier). Group PAT tells a different story: it actually FELL 28.9% YoY (LKR 2.49bn vs LKR 3.51bn in Q2 2025), even though Group Revenue (+24% YoY) and Group Operating Profit (+35% YoY) both grew nicely. The reason is a single line: Group \"Fair Value Gain\" on investment property was LKR 1.09bn this quarter vs an unusually large LKR 2.33bn in Q2 2025 -- last year's comparative quarter had an outsized one-off property revaluation gain that simply didn't repeat. Strip that out and the underlying Group operating business (leasing/property trading/services) is growing at a healthy double-digit clip; the YoY PAT decline is a base-effect from a non-recurring gain, not a deterioration in the core business. QoQ, Group PAT rose 35.9% (LKR 1.83bn derived Q1 2026 to LKR 2.49bn Q2 2026), consistent with the improving operating trend. Group leverage also improved: Debt/Equity fell to 0.15x from 0.20x, and Interest Cover rose to 20x from 17x.", "source_doc_id": "52052", "source_page": 4, "gaps_note": "Q1 2026 figures used for the QoQ comparison are DERIVED (Six Months Ended 30/06/2026 cumulative minus the separately-disclosed Quarter Ended 30/06/2026), not a directly disclosed line. Extraction scope for this update is revenue/PAT/EPS/gross and operating profit/margins only (no balance sheet or full cash flow detail), per current project scope.", "qoq": [{"metric": "tax_expense", "label": "Tax Expense", "prior_period_label": "Q1 2026 (quarter ended 31 March 2026, derived)", "prior_value": 92344.0, "new_period_label": "Q2 2026 (quarter ended 30 June 2026)", "new_value": 349714.0, "pct_change": 2.787078749025383, "direction": "improved"}, {"metric": "profit_before_tax", "label": "Profit Before Tax", 